    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "lol yeah, whispers and drafts that move the wrong way sounds spooky. i actually had a tenant tell me something similar last week. they were saying it felt like there was something small and mischievous hiding in the vents, like they could actually hear little footsteps or scratching that didn't sound like rats. \n\ndo you think there's any truth to those kinds of stories? like, could there be something out there—maybe something small or even a bit \"nuisance-like\"—that people mistake for a mechanical glitch?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those stories of tiny, mischievous things in the vents are quite common, and honestly, it's often a case of misinterpretation, not actual spectral activity. It's much more likely to be a small creature, like a very bold mouse or even a family of field mice, nesting in the ductwork or near the unit. These little critters can certainly make sounds that mimic footsteps or scratching, which sounds much more like a very persistent, tiny infestation than anything supernatural. I've seen enough debris and nesting material to back up that theory more times than I can count!",
      "source": "target",
